{"reason": "The current model freezes the entire DeBERTa backbone, causing validation loss oscillations and early stopping at epoch 10 with best log-loss 0.474. Such overfitting and convergence issues were resolved in similar successful experiments by unfreezing top layers, using differential learning rates, and applying OneCycleLR with warmup. Conversely, adding engineered features or complex architectures failed. Thus, I focus on model_design (unfreeze layers, custom head) and training_evaluation (optimizer groups, OneCycleLR). data_processing remains unchanged.", "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"model_design": "Change 1: Unfreeze last 6 transformer layers of DeBERTa-v3-large. In __init__, after freezing all backbone parameters, iterate over backbone.deberta.encoder.layer[-6:] and set requires_grad=True. Keep pooling/attention/classifier trainable. Change 2: Retain custom pooling and attention modules as they are. WHY: Unfreezing top layers allows task-specific adaptation while preserving pretrained knowledge, preventing overfitting. Historical successful experiments (end-to-end fine-tuning) achieved better performance. HOW: directly modify SpookyAuthorClassifier.__init__ to enable training on top layers. Interface: all forward signatures preserved.", "training_evaluation": "Change 1: Reorganize optimizer groups: backbone unfrozen params (lr=2e-5), custom head (pool+attention+classifier) params (lr=5e-5). Add weight_decay=0.01 only for non-bias/norm. Use betas=(0.9,0.98) for head group. Change 2: Replace CosineAnnealingLR with OneCycleLR(max_lr=[2e-5,5e-5], pct_start=0.1, final_div_factor=100). WHY: Differential LRs prevent catastrophic forgetting; OneCycleLR's warmup stabilizes new head training and improves convergence, as seen in successful experiments. HOW: modify optimizer definition and scheduler instantiation after train_loader is created (since total_steps depends on it). Ensure scheduler.step() called per batch instead of per epoch. Preserve early stopping and metric tracking."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
